  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 442 AM CDT Wed Oct 7 2026\n\nToday through Tuesday:\n\nHot and dry conditions are expected to continue through Thursday. \nWith Isaias expected to strengthen by to hurricane by Thursday, \nbreezy conditions will be added to hot/dry conditions in place. as a \nresult, there is a potential for fire weather concerns on Thursday \nand Friday. \n\nTropical Depression #9 has now developed into Tropical Storm Isaias \nin the southwestern Gulf. NHC also expects Isaias to undergo rapid \nstrengthening over the next day or two, becoming a hurricane by \nThursday. NHC expect Isaias to move east-northeast, turning \nnorthward towards the MS/AL coastline by Thursday-Friday. Greatest \nimpacts are expected along the coast, however, inland rain/wind \nthreats will be possible in central/eastern portions MS starting \nFriday night through Saturday night. With the center more likely to \nbe to the east, any low end tornado threats would likely be to our \neast of the CWA. Please continue to monitor for future updates.\n\nOnce TC Isaias progress away from the area, hot and dry conditions \nwill return as high pressure builds over the region. /SW/EC/",
